    {
      "question": "e-11048",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "37f7c64e553483e179297863d1fd20a01b75591560e419021f727e18b03775ce",
      "new_sha256": "cb857cb7d56cfa548e8d97829e44f7e8dc2e1de400f2157d59cc83f475a068f0",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-11048",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(y-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(y-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(y-{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(1)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot 0-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,9)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,9) & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{9-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11048.json",
          "file_sha256": "7e8c7140306fb9e32cf83b258ca5279043f1e23ed343c1e88364d8c684119034"
        }
