      "new_sha256": "d20a19b8c0b7a6fe1249adad30791b402a69051aaf9b5f18a78dc3c2011a9813",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-11112",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{4x-y}{x+{y}^{2}}) & =\\frac{\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(4x-y)\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x+{y}^{2})}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot 1}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x+4{y}^{2}-4x+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}{|}_{(2,-1)} & =\\frac{4(-1)^{2}+(-1)}{{(2+{(-1)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
